<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 9 December, from 536 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belisarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">536 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,490 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belisarius enters Rome unopposed as the Gothic garrison withdraws</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The citizens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, mindful of the fate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, put up no resistance to Justinian's general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a>, and the 4,000-strong Gothic garrison withdrew. Belisarius went on to take Ravenna in 540.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">730 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,296 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Khazars destroy an Umayyad army at Marj Ardabil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> army led by Barjik destroyed the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and killed their commander, al-Jarrah ibn Abdallah al-Hakami. The Khazars then raided deep into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> as far as northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-ardabil">Battle of Marj Ardabil</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1165">1165 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">861 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malcolm IV, the 'Maiden King' of Scotland, dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malcolm IV died unmarried at 24, after a reign in which he surrendered Northumbria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumbria">Cumbria</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a>. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-lion">William the Lion</a> succeeded him and reigned for 49 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1531">1531 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Diego reports a vision of the Virgin at Tepeyac</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to tradition, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a> appeared to the Indigenous convert <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-diego">Juan Diego</a> on the hill of Tepeyac near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>. The image of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/our-lady-of-guadalupe">Our Lady of Guadalupe</a> became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s most revered religious symbol.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1688">1688 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">338 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Williamite dragoons rout an Irish Army detachment at Reading</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> States Army dragoons under Hans Bentinck, supported by Williamite civilians, routed an Irish Army detachment under Patrick Sarsfield from Reading in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berkshire">Berkshire</a>. It was one of only two substantial battles fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-england">William III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jerusalem surrenders to British forces</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> surrendered the city to the British army, ending four centuries of Ottoman rule. General Allenby entered on foot two days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British forces launch Operation Compass in Egypt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and Commonwealth troops attacked Italian camps in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. In two months they advanced 500 miles and took some 130,000 prisoners, before Rommel's arrival turned the tide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tanganyika becomes independent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tanganyika became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> as prime minister. In 1964 it united with Zanzibar to form Tanzania.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 9 December <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-de-porres"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-de-porres.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martin de Porres</span><span class="tp">1579–1639</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-papagos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexandros-papagos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexandros Papagos</span><span class="tp">1883–1955</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bob-hawke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bob-hawke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bob Hawke</span><span class="tp">1929–2019</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 9 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sigismund, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1368–1437</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-iv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Pius IV</span><span class="tp">1499–1565</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-hyde-1st-earl-of-clarendon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-hyde-1st-earl-of-clarendon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Hyde, 1st Earl of Clarendon</span><span class="tp">1609–1674</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tarabai"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tarabai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tarabai</span><span class="tp">1675–1761</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-baldwin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-baldwin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Baldwin</span><span class="tp">1804–1858</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
